<title>UK: Britain sees downside of &quot;hire and fire&quot; at Ford.</title>
<headline>Britain sees downside of &quot;hire and fire&quot; at Ford.</headline>
<byline>Alan Raybould</byline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-01-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>As unemployment has dropped in Britain over the past four years, the British government has boasted about its flexible labour market and railed against the strictures of the European Union's Social Chapter.</p>
<p>But the announcement by U.S. car giant Ford of massive job cuts at its Halewood plant in northwest England has brought it home -- for the workers at least -- that flexibility means being able to fire, as well as hire, unencumbered by red tape.</p>
</text>
